  "answer": "No, please don't use an impact driver. The installation instructions specifically say not to. Use an electric screwdriver with Allen (hex) bits, or a standard bike multitool. The screws only need to be finger tight. For example, the brackets are secured with a 4 mm Allen key and the bike racks are attached finger-tight only, so an impact driver could easily overtighten them.",
